      "message": "fix(motion,app): a turning pass that ends inside a longer bar leaves its cut at feed\n\nEach profile ride ends at its window's top with a radial move out. When\nthe bar runs on past that end - a bar longer than the part, or a window\nthat stops partway along it - the nose sits inside the bar's uncut end,\nand that move was a rapid through stock: the meridian law flagged one\nRapidInStock per rung and the post was refused.\n\n- StockEnv carries the bar's far end (s_top), read from the stock in\n  the part's frame (turning_stock::read).\n- StockEnv::runs_past says when the bar goes on past a ride's end.\n- prof::ride takes an Exit: Rapid as before, or Feed at the plunge feed\n  when the bar runs past. Profile rough and finish choose it from the\n  stock; the contour kinds, which read no stock, keep Rapid.\n- A bar that ends with the part keeps the exact old path.\n\nFixes #229\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
